=== ev-introducer
_note: The introducer-relationship event. Reachable from week 4 on via genericEvents. Deliberately a squeeze rather than a favour: the member is carrying real risk and asking the player to absorb some of it, which is what rapport actually buys.
talks: rep-x=talk-rep, sen-x=talk-sen, office
actions: lobby, push

--- start
REP-X: They catch you before the elevator, holding a marked-up copy of your own bill. "Leadership's office called. Not about your bill — about me." A committee assignment, a district project, a favour owed; the specifics don't matter and they don't offer them. "They'd like to know if I'm carrying this all the way or just filing it. I have to give them an answer this week, and whatever I say, I have to live in this building afterward."
PROCEDURE: This is the pressure that never appears in a journal entry. No vote, no record — just a member deciding how much of their own year to spend on you.
TALK STORY: They came to you first. That is the whole tell. Somebody who had already folded would have sent an email on Friday.
BASE BUILDING: If the answer is 'you're on your own,' you don't get a second one of these. Members talk to each other more than they talk to us.

* "Tell them you're carrying it. We'll put people in your district behind you."
  {+10 house, +2 support, -3 influence}
  They exhale. "Then I'll say yes." You have just promised turnout in a district you do not organize yet, which is a problem for a future week and a real one.

* "Say whatever keeps you safe. I'd rather have you in April."
  {+4 house, +2 influence}
  "...Thank you." Nobody in this hallway says that to a member, and it costs the bill something this week — but they will still be picking up the phone in April, which is more than most advocates can say.

* [PROCEDURE 13 red] "Ask them to put that request in writing."
  mods: influence/25, TALK STORY/4
  pass:
    {+8 house, +3 influence, flag nothing-in-writing}
    Rep. X actually laughs. "They will never do that." Which is the point, and they see it a beat later: a request nobody will write down is a request nobody can enforce. The call is not returned, and the bill keeps its number.
  fail:
    {-8 house, -2 influence}
    "That's how you talk to an agency, not to the people who set my committee." They put the marked-up copy back in their bag. "I'll handle it my way." You do not learn what their way was.
